{"response":{"docs":[{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MICRO_0001709","ontology_name":"micro","ontology_prefix":"MICRO","short_form":"MICRO_0001709","broad_synonyms":["bovine serum"],"description":[],"label":"calf serum","obo_id":"MICRO:0001709","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["new borne calf serum"]},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D012710","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["Albumin Bovine","Albumin, Bovine Serum","Albumin, Bovine","Bovine Albumin","Bovine Serum Albumin","Bovine Serum, Fetal","Bovine, Albumin","Calf Serum, Fetal","Fetal Bovine Serum","Fetal Calf Serum","Serum, Fetal Bovine","Serum, Fetal Calf"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_D012710","description":["Serum albumin from cows, commonly used in in vitro biological studies. (From Stedman, 25th ed)"],"label":"Serum Albumin, Bovine","obo_id":"mesh:D012710","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MICRO_0001660","ontology_name":"micro","ontology_prefix":"MICRO","short_form":"MICRO_0001660","description":[],"label":"fetal calf serum","obo_id":"MICRO:0001660","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C113696","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C113696","description":["The serum blood fraction obtained from cow fetuses and used as a component of growth medium."],"label":"Fetal Bovine Serum","obo_id":"NCIT:C113696","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["FBS","FCS","Fetal Bovine Serum","Fetal Calf Serum"]},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/C088695","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["ActoHorm"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_C088695","description":[],"label":"deproteinized calf blood serum","obo_id":"mesh:C088695","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/XCO_0000989","ontology_name":"xco","ontology_prefix":"XCO","short_form":"XCO_0000989","description":["This is any experimental condition in which the main influencing factor is fetal bovine serum. Fetal bovine serum is the most widely used serum-supplement for the in vitro cell culture of eukaryotic cells. Fetal bovine serum is derived from the blood drawn from a bovine fetus via a closed system of collection at a slaughterhouse."],"label":"fetal bovine serum","obo_id":"XCO:0000989","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["FBS","fetal calf serum"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MSIO_0000017","ontology_name":"msio","ontology_prefix":"MSIO","short_form":"MSIO_0000017","description":["Fetal bovine serum (FBS) or fetal calf serum (spelled foetal in Commonwealth English) is a material entity which correspsonds to the blood fraction remaining after the natural coagulation of blood, followed by centrifugation to remove any remaining red blood cells."],"label":"fetal bovine serum","obo_id":"MSIO:0000017","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C29187","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C29187","description":["A cancer vaccine consisting of a recombinant vaccinia virus encoding the tumor-associated gene MAGE-1 that is contaminated with bovine viral diarrhea virus (BVDV).  The MAGE-1 gene is a member of the melanoma antigen-encoding gene family which is expressed in various malignant tumors such as hepatocellular carcinoma and germ cell tumors in addition to melanoma.  Vaccination with vaccinia virus expressing human MAGE-1 may generate antitumoral T-cell responses.  BVDV is an RNA pestivirus that may contaminate vaccines due to its presence in the fetal calf serum used as a growth supplement in the tissue culture of mammalian cells used in vaccine production. (NCI04)"],"label":"MAGE-1 Vaccinia Contaminated with BVDV","obo_id":"NCIT:C29187","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["MAGE-1 Vaccinia Contaminated with BVDV"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C29476","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C29476","description":["A cancer vaccine consisting of a recombinant vector encoding the tumor-associated carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) that is contaminated with bovine viral diarrhea virus (BVDV). The carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) is a prevalent tumor marker expressed by a number of different cancers such as colorectal, breast, lung and ovarian carcinomas; vaccination with vaccinia virus genetically engineered to express CEA may generate antitumoral T-cell responses. BVDV is an RNA pestivirus that may contaminate vaccines due to its presence in fetal calf serum used as a growth supplement in the tissue culture of mammalian cells used in vaccine production. (NCI04)"],"label":"TBC-CEA-Contaminated W/ BVDV","obo_id":"NCIT:C29476","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["TBC-CEA-Contaminated W/ BVDV"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0007049","ontology_name":"vo","ontology_prefix":"VO","short_form":"VO_0007049","description":["A cancer vaccine consisting of a recombinant vector encoding the tumor-associated carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) that is‚Äö√†√∂‚àö¬ßcontaminated‚Äö√†√∂‚àö¬ßwith bovine viral diarrhea virus (BVDV). The carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) is a prevalent tumor marker expressed by a number of different cancers such as colorectal, breast, lung and ovarian carcinomas; vaccination with vaccinia virus genetically engineered to express‚Äö√†√∂‚àö¬ßCEA‚Äö√†√∂‚àö¬ßmay generate antitumoral T-cell responses.‚Äö√†√∂‚àö¬ßBVDV‚Äö√†√∂‚àö¬ßis an RNA pestivirus that may contaminate vaccines due to its presence in fetal calf serum used as a growth supplement in the tissue culture of mammalian cells used in vaccine production.","Gene name: MBL2"],"label":"TBC-CEA-Contaminated W/ BVDV vaccine","obo_id":"VO:0007049","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0007538","ontology_name":"vo","ontology_prefix":"VO","short_form":"VO_0007538","description":["A cancer vaccine consisting of a recombinant vaccinia virus encoding the tumor-associated gene MAGE-1 that is contaminated with bovine viral diarrhea virus (BVDV). The MAGE-1 gene is a member of the melanoma antigen-encoding gene family which is expressed in various malignant tumors such as hepatocellular carcinoma and germ cell tumors in addition to melanoma. Vaccination with vaccinia virus expressing human MAGE-1 may generate antitumoral T-cell responses. BVDV is an RNA pestivirus that may contaminate vaccines due to its presence in the fetal calf serum used as a growth supplement in the tissue culture of mammalian cells used in vaccine production.","Gene name: MAGEA1"],"label":"MAGE-1 Vaccinia contaminated with bovine viral diarrhea virus vaccine","obo_id":"VO:0007538","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0013297","ontology_name":"mondo","related_synonyms":["muscular dystrophy, limb-girdle, type 1H","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 1H"],"ontology_prefix":"MONDO","short_form":"MONDO_0013297","description":["Autosomal dominant limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 1H (LGMD1H) is a subtype of autosomal dominant limb-girdle muscular dystrophy characterized by slowly progressive proximal muscular weakness initially affecting the lower limbs (and later involving the upper limbs), hypotrophy of upper and lower limb-girdle muscles, hyporeflexia, calf hypertrophy, and increased serum creatine kinase. There is no involvement of oculo-facial-bulbar muscles and cardiac muscle."],"label":"autosomal dominant limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 1H","obo_id":"MONDO:0013297","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["LGMD1H"]},{"iri":"http://www.orpha.net/ORDO/Orphanet_565899","ontology_name":"ordo","ontology_prefix":"ORDO","short_form":"ORDO_565899","description":["A rare autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy characterized by infantile to adolescent onset of a milder form of limb-girdle muscular dystrophy with or without intellectual disability. Patients present variable proximal limb muscular weakness with calf hypertrophy and elevated serum creatine kinase."],"label":"POMGNT2-related limb-girdle muscular dystrophy R24","obo_id":"ORDO:565899","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0009676","ontology_name":"mondo","related_synonyms":["muscular dystrophy, limb-girdle, type 2B","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy, type 2B"],"ontology_prefix":"MONDO","short_form":"MONDO_0009676","description":["Autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2B (LGMD2B) is a subtype of autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy characterized by an onset in late adolescence or early adulthood of slowly progressive, proximal weakness and atrophy of shoulder and pelvic girdle muscles. Cardiac and respiratory muscles are not involved. Hypertrophy of the calf muscles and highly elevated serum creatine kinase levels are frequently observed."],"label":"autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2B","obo_id":"MONDO:0009676","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["DYSF autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy","LGMD2B","LGMD3","autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy caused by mutation in DYSF","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy due to dysferlin deficiency","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2B","muscular dystrophy, limb-girdle, autosomal recessive 2"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018098","ontology_name":"mondo","related_synonyms":["limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 1E"],"ontology_prefix":"MONDO","short_form":"MONDO_0018098","description":["Terminology notes: See comments for LGMD1D","Autosomal dominant limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 1E (LGMD1E) is a subtype of autosomal dominant limb-girdle muscular dystrophy characterized by an adult onset of progressive cardiac conduction defects that begin with cardiac dysrhythmia. Congestive heart failure and symptoms of progressive muscle weakness (present in a proximal distribution) tend to occur later. Affected patients may present only the cardiac features of the disease. Additional features include exertional dyspnea, calf hypertrophy, elevated creatine kinase serum levels and muscle cytoplasmic inclusions."],"label":"autosomal dominant limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 1E (DES)","obo_id":"MONDO:0018098","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["LGMD1E"]},{"iri":"http://www.orpha.net/ORDO/Orphanet_268","ontology_name":"ordo","ontology_prefix":"ORDO","short_form":"ORDO_268","description":["A subtype of autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy characterized by an onset in late adolescence or early adulthood of slowly progressive, proximal weakness and atrophy of shoulder and pelvic girdle muscles. Cardiac and respiratory muscles are not involved. Hypertrophy of the calf muscles and highly elevated serum creatine kinase levels are frequently observed."],"label":"Dysferlin-related limb-girdle muscular dystrophy R2","obo_id":"ORDO:268","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0011028","ontology_name":"mondo","related_synonyms":["limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2F","muscular dystrophy limb-girdle with delta-sarcoglyan deficiency","muscular dystrophy, limb-girdle, type 2F"],"ontology_prefix":"MONDO","short_form":"MONDO_0011028","broad_synonyms":["delta-sarcoglycanopathy"],"description":["Autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2F (LGMD2F) is a subtype of autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy characterized by a variable age of onset of progressive weakness and wasting of the proximal skeletal muscles of the shoulder and pelvic girdles, frequently associated with progressive respiratory muscle impairment and cardiomyopathy. Calf hypertrophy, muscle cramps and elevated serum creatine kinase levels are also observed. Neuropsychomotor development is usually normal."],"label":"autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2F","obo_id":"MONDO:0011028","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["LGMD2F","SGCD autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy","autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy caused by mutation in SGCD","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy due to delta-sarcoglycan deficiency","muscular dystrophy, limb-girdle, autosomal recessive 6"]},{"iri":"http://www.orpha.net/ORDO/Orphanet_219","ontology_name":"ordo","ontology_prefix":"ORDO","short_form":"ORDO_219","description":["A subtype of autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy characterized by a variable age of onset of progressive weakness and wasting of the proximal skeletal muscles of the shoulder and pelvic girdles, frequently associated with progressive respiratory muscle impairment and cardiomyopathy. Calf hypertrophy, muscle cramps and elevated serum creatine kinase levels are also observed. Neuropsychomotor development is usually normal."],"label":"Delta-sarcoglycan-related limb-girdle muscular dystrophy R6","obo_id":"ORDO:219","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0009677","ontology_name":"mondo","related_synonyms":["limb-girdle muscular dystrophy with gamma-sarcoglycan deficiency","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy, type 2C"],"ontology_prefix":"MONDO","short_form":"MONDO_0009677","description":["Autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2C (LGMD2C) is a subtype of autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy characterized by a childhood onset of progressive shoulder and pelvic girdle muscle weakness and atrophy frequently associated with calf hypertrophy, diaphragmatic weakness, and/or variable cardiac abnormalities. Mild to moderate elevated serum creatine kinase levels and positive Gowers sign are reported."],"label":"autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2C","obo_id":"MONDO:0009677","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["DMDA1","LGMD2C","Maghrebian myopathy","SCARMD","SGCG autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy","autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy caused by mutation in SGCG","autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2C","gamma-sarcoglycanopathy","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy due to gamma-sarcoglycan deficiency","muscular dystrophy, limb-girdle, autosomal recessive 5","muscular dystrophy, limb-girdle, type 2C"]},{"iri":"http://www.orpha.net/ORDO/Orphanet_353","ontology_name":"ordo","ontology_prefix":"ORDO","short_form":"ORDO_353","description":["A subtype of autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy characterized by a childhood onset of progressive shoulder and pelvic girdle muscle weakness and atrophy frequently associated with calf hypertrophy, diaphragmatic weakness, and/or variable cardiac abnormalities. Mild to moderate elevated serum creatine kinase levels and positive Gowers sign are reported."],"label":"Gamma-sarcoglycan-related limb-girdle muscular dystrophy R5","obo_id":"ORDO:353","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0011787","ontology_name":"mondo","related_synonyms":["muscular dystrophy-dystroglycanopathy (limb-girdle), type C, 5","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2I"],"ontology_prefix":"MONDO","short_form":"MONDO_0011787","description":["A subtype of autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy that presents a highly variable age of onset and phenotypic spectrum typically characterized by slowly progressive proximal weakness of the pelvic and shoulder girdle musculature (predominantly affecting the lower limbs), frequently associated with waddling gait, scapular winging, calf and tongue hypertrophy, exercise-induced myalgia, and myoglobinuria and/or elevated creatine kinase serum levels. Abdominal muscle weakness, cardiomyopathy, respiratory muscle involvement and various brain abnormalities have also been reported."],"label":"autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2I","obo_id":"MONDO:0011787","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["muscular dystrophy-dystroglycanopathy (limb-girdle), type C5","FKRP autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy","LGMD-FKRP related","LGMD2I","MDDGC5","autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy caused by mutation in FKRP","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy due to FKRP deficiency","muscular dystrophy-dystroglycanopathy (Limb-girdle) type C, 5"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0013686","ontology_name":"mondo","related_synonyms":["myopathy, distal, Tateyama type","MPDT"],"ontology_prefix":"MONDO","short_form":"MONDO_0013686","description":["Distal myopathy, Tateyama type is a rare, genetic, slowly progressive, distal myopathy disorder characterized by muscle atrophy and weakness limited to the small muscles of the hands and feet (in particular, thenar and hypothenar muscle atrophy), increased serum creatine kinase, and severely reduced caveolin-3 expression on muscle biopsy. Some patients may also show calf hypertrophy, pes cavus, and signs of muscle hyperexcitability."],"label":"distal myopathy, Tateyama type","obo_id":"MONDO:0013686","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://www.orpha.net/ORDO/Orphanet_488650","ontology_name":"ordo","ontology_prefix":"ORDO","short_form":"ORDO_488650","description":["Distal myopathy, Tateyama type is a rare, genetic, slowly progressive, distal myopathy disorder characterized by muscle atrophy and weakness limited to the small muscles of the hands and feet (in particular, thenar and hypothenar muscle atrophy), increased serum creatine kinase, and severely reduced caveolin-3 expression on muscle biopsy. Some patients may also show calf hypertrophy, pes cavus, and signs of muscle hyperexcitability."],"label":"Distal myopathy, Tateyama type","obo_id":"ORDO:488650","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://www.orpha.net/ORDO/Orphanet_34515","ontology_name":"ordo","ontology_prefix":"ORDO","short_form":"ORDO_34515","description":["A form of autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy that presents a highly variable age of onset and phenotypic spectrum typically characterized by slowly progressive proximal weakness of the pelvic and shoulder girdle musculature (predominantly affecting the lower limbs), frequently associated with waddling gait, scapular winging, calf and tongue hypertrophy, exercise-induced myalgia, abdominal muscle weakness, cardiomyopathy, respiratory muscle involvement, and myoglobinuria and/or elevated creatine kinase serum levels."],"label":"FKRP-related limb-girdle muscular dystrophy R9","obo_id":"ORDO:34515","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://livercancer.imbi.uni-heidelberg.de/ccont#CCONT_0000049","ontology_name":"enm","ontology_prefix":"ENM","short_form":"CCONT_0000049","description":[],"label":"bovine calf serum","obo_id":"CCONT:0000049","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://livercancer.imbi.uni-heidelberg.de/ccont#CCONT_0000051","ontology_name":"enm","ontology_prefix":"ENM","short_form":"CCONT_0000051","description":[],"label":"newborn calf serum","obo_id":"CCONT:0000051","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0013297","ontology_name":"efo","related_synonyms":["muscular dystrophy, limb-girdle, type 1H","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 1H"],"ontology_prefix":"EFO","short_form":"MONDO_0013297","description":["Autosomal dominant limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 1H (LGMD1H) is a subtype of autosomal dominant limb-girdle muscular dystrophy characterized by slowly progressive proximal muscular weakness initially affecting the lower limbs (and later involving the upper limbs), hypotrophy of upper and lower limb-girdle muscles, hyporeflexia, calf hypertrophy, and increased serum creatine kinase. There is no involvement of oculo-facial-bulbar muscles and cardiac muscle."],"label":"autosomal dominant limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 1H","obo_id":"MONDO:0013297","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["LGMD1H"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0009676","ontology_name":"efo","related_synonyms":["muscular dystrophy, limb-girdle, type 2B","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy, type 2B"],"ontology_prefix":"EFO","short_form":"MONDO_0009676","description":["Autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2B (LGMD2B) is a subtype of autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy characterized by an onset in late adolescence or early adulthood of slowly progressive, proximal weakness and atrophy of shoulder and pelvic girdle muscles. Cardiac and respiratory muscles are not involved. Hypertrophy of the calf muscles and highly elevated serum creatine kinase levels are frequently observed."],"label":"autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2B","obo_id":"MONDO:0009676","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["DYSF autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy","LGMD2B","LGMD3","autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy caused by mutation in DYSF","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy due to dysferlin deficiency","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2B","muscular dystrophy, limb-girdle, autosomal recessive 2"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018098","ontology_name":"efo","related_synonyms":["limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 1E"],"ontology_prefix":"EFO","short_form":"MONDO_0018098","description":["Autosomal dominant limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 1E (LGMD1E) is a subtype of autosomal dominant limb-girdle muscular dystrophy characterized by an adult onset of progressive cardiac conduction defects that begin with cardiac dysrhythmia. Congestive heart failure and symptoms of progressive muscle weakness (present in a proximal distribution) tend to occur later. Affected patients may present only the cardiac features of the disease. Additional features include exertional dyspnea, calf hypertrophy, elevated creatine kinase serum levels and muscle cytoplasmic inclusions."],"label":"autosomal dominant limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 1E (DES)","obo_id":"MONDO:0018098","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["LGMD1E"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0011028","ontology_name":"efo","related_synonyms":["limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2F","muscular dystrophy limb-girdle with delta-sarcoglyan deficiency","muscular dystrophy, limb-girdle, type 2F"],"ontology_prefix":"EFO","short_form":"MONDO_0011028","broad_synonyms":["delta-sarcoglycanopathy"],"description":["Autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2F (LGMD2F) is a subtype of autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy characterized by a variable age of onset of progressive weakness and wasting of the proximal skeletal muscles of the shoulder and pelvic girdles, frequently associated with progressive respiratory muscle impairment and cardiomyopathy. Calf hypertrophy, muscle cramps and elevated serum creatine kinase levels are also observed. Neuropsychomotor development is usually normal."],"label":"autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2F","obo_id":"MONDO:0011028","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["LGMD2F","SGCD autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy","autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy caused by mutation in SGCD","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy due to delta-sarcoglycan deficiency","muscular dystrophy, limb-girdle, autosomal recessive 6"]}],"numFound":32,"start":0},"responseHeader":{"QTime":0,"status":0},"facet_counts":{"facet_fields":{"ontologyPreferredPrefix":["MONDO","7","EFO","6","ORDO","6","NCIT","3","MICRO","2","mesh","2","ENM","2","VO","2","XCO","1","MSIO","1"],"isDefiningOntology":["true","24","false","8"],"ontologyId":["mondo","7","efo","6","ordo","6","ncit","3","micro","2","mesh","2","enm","2","vo","2","xco","1","msio","1"],"ontologyIri":["http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/mondo-international.owl","7","https://www.orphadata.com/data/ontologies/ordo/last_version/ORDO_en_4.9.owl","6","http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/efo.owl","6","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ncit.owl","3","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/vo.owl","2","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MicrO.owl","2","http://enanomapper.github.io/ontologies/enanomapper.owl","2","https://w3id.org/biopragmatics/resources/mesh/mesh.ofn","2","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/xco.owl","1","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/msio.owl","1"],"isObsolete":["false","32"],"type":["class","32"]}}}